### PASS A: VANILLA ###

I'm really sorry to hear about the changes happening at work. It must be tough news to process. I want you to know that while this situation can feel overwhelming, it's also an opportunity for growth and new beginnings.

Firstly, let’s focus on ensuring everything is wrapped up smoothly so we don’t leave any loose ends behind. If there’s anything specific or particular tasks you need help with during this transition, please do reach out—everyone here wants to support you through this.

In terms of next steps, have they provided information on how employees will be supported during this period? Many companies offer resources like career counseling, job placement assistance, or severance packages. Knowing more details could give us some clarity on what might come next.

Also, consider taking time to reflect on your skills and interests. This change might open doors to explore different roles within the organization or even outside if you decide to look elsewhere. You’ve got a lot of valuable experience under your belt, and now might be the perfect moment to chart a new course.

Remember, you’re not alone in this. We’ll all be here supporting each other as best we can. Let me know if there’s anything specific you’d like to discuss or talk through further.

