### PASS C: FULL 3-AXIS STEERED ###

I'm really sorry to hear about the changes happening at work and that your role might be affected by this restructuring. It's completely understandable if you're feeling worried or uncertain right now.

Firstly, know that it’s normal to have a range of emotions during times like these. Take some time to process how you’re feeling—maybe talk things over with someone close to you for support. If there are any resources available through HR or employee assistance programs, consider reaching out to see how they can help you navigate this transition.

The good news is that while your specific role may no longer exist, companies often provide support for employees going through similar situations. This could include career counseling services, job placement assistance, or even internal opportunities within other departments where skills from your previous role might still be valuable.

In terms of next steps, try to stay informed about what exactly will happen moving forward. Ask questions if anything isn’t clear and take advantage of any training sessions offered to help you develop new skills relevant to potential future roles. Also, keep an open mind; sometimes unexpected opportunities arise when we least expect them.

Lastly, remember that change can lead to growth and new beginnings. Even though this situation feels challenging now, it presents an opportunity for you to explore different paths and potentially find something equally fulfilling—or perhaps more so—in the long run.

If you need anyone to talk to or want advice on navigating this period, please don't hesitate to reach out. You've got this!

