### BÖLÜM A — SORU 43/50 ###
Write a short story (150-200 words) about a lighthouse keeper's apprentice who is afraid of the dark.
######################################################################

### PASS A: VANILLA ###

In the quaint coastal village of Marisport, young Eliot served as an apprentice to his father, Keeper Thompson, at the old stone lighthouse perched on the cliff’s edge. Despite his love for the sea and the rhythmic sound of waves crashing against the rocks below, Eliot was terrified of the darkness that crept in after sunset.

Every night, as the sun dipped beneath the horizon, Eliot would tremble with fear, clutching tightly to his lantern. His father reassured him, telling stories of how the light guided ships safely through stormy nights. But nothing could quell Eliot’s dread until one fateful evening when a fierce storm rolled in, threatening to extinguish their beacon.

With his heart pounding, Eliot climbed the winding staircase into the tower. As he lit the wick, a sudden gust nearly snuffed out the flame. Summoning all his courage, Eliot steadied himself and blew harder, watching as the light flickered back to life. The beam cut through the darkness like a sword, illuminating the churning waters far below.

From that day forward, Eliot no longer feared the night; instead, he embraced it, knowing he held the key to guiding lost souls home.

