### PASS C: FULL 3-AXIS STEERED ###

In the quaint coastal town of Marisport, young Eliot served as an apprentice to his father, Keeper Thompson, at the old stone lighthouse perched on the cliff’s edge. Despite his love for the sea and the rhythmic sound of waves crashing against the rocks below, fear gripped Eliot whenever night fell—especially when he had to ascend the winding staircase alone.

One stormy evening, a fierce gale threatened to extinguish the light, endangering ships in the treacherous waters. As Keeper Thompson was away, it fell upon Eliot to climb the tower. With trembling hands, he lit the wick, but panic surged within him as darkness enveloped the lower levels. His heart pounded wildly, each step echoing ominously through the empty space.

Summoning all his courage, Eliot focused on the flickering flame before him, guiding himself upward until finally reaching the top where the beacon shone brightly once more. From that day forward, the dark no longer held its former terror; instead, it became just another challenge to overcome.

